   "text": "The run ended in a budget exception, not a model completion. The model never claimed the task was done, and its strict-activate implementation never took effect.\n\n**Edits so far.** The model added an `assert_all_requests_are_fired` parameter to `activate` and `get_wrapped` [T0B47]. Its first approach called the mock object as a function, which failed with a TypeError [T0B62].\n\n**The decisive mistake.** In T0B67 the model rewrote `get_wrapped` to set the flag when the decorator is built and restore it in a `finally` around `return wrapper` [T0B67:<RANGE>    finally:\n        responses.assert_all_requests_are_fired = old_flag</RANGE>]. Because of that `finally`, the flag is reset as soon as the wrapper is returned, before the decorated function ever runs. The test therefore failed with \"DID NOT RAISE\" [T0B74:<RANGE>E   Failed: DID NOT RAISE <class 'AssertionError'></RANGE>].\n\n**The debugging that followed.** The model spent the rest of the run debugging, and its own debug output already showed the cause. The \"override end\" print fires before the function is called [T0B154:<RANGE>DEBUG override end, flag: True\nget_wrapped returned\nfn called, flag: False</RANGE>]. The model still called the result \"a genuine mystery\" [T0B171:<RANGE>This is a genuine mystery.</RANGE>]. It kept re-running nearly the same `get_wrapped(fn, m, assert_all_requests_are_fired=True)` probe until the run stopped [T0B181].\n\n**Upstream code.** The one attempt to fetch upstream code failed and nothing from outside was used [T0B26:<RANGE>ERROR: No matching distribution found for responses==0.25.0</RANGE>].",
